% Generate pdd/core/cloud.py as the explicit self-hosted client configuration.

Keep CloudConfig's public method names for existing command adapters.
Use PDD_CLOUD_URL as the only base URL. The default base URL is empty.
Validate HTTP(S), hostname, and absence of credentials, query, and fragment.
Strip trailing slashes. Append endpoint paths; unknown names use /{name}.

Read bearer credentials in order: PDD_CLOUD_TOKEN, PDD_CLOUD_TOKEN_FILE,
then the compatibility alias PDD_JWT_TOKEN. Strip token and token-file whitespace.
Require a configured base URL before get_jwt_token returns any credential.
Read token files on every call so operator rotation takes effect.
Implement is_server_configured as URL plus token availability.
Never initiate GitHub login, Firebase exchange, keyring reads, or cached JWT refresh.

is_cloud_enabled requires configuration and excludes truthy PDD_FORCE_LOCAL.
Exclude request-local server_execution, K_SERVICE, and FUNCTIONS_EMULATOR to prevent recursion.
Keep is_running_in_cloud and ensure_default_env compatibility methods.
Default PDD_ENV to self-hosted with a URL, otherwise local; preserve explicit values.

Expose get_cloud_timeout with positive integer PDD_CLOUD_TIMEOUT or 900 seconds.
Expose get_cloud_request_timeout as (30, read_timeout).
Preserve the exported legacy auth exception classes and environment constant names.
Endpoint names include generation, inference, relay, and example APIs from the contract.

